# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, a contributor whose editor writes LF and one whose editor writes
# CRLF produce commits where git sees every line of a file as changed. That is
# what turned the shared-UI merge into whole-file conflicts: UserFormLayer.tsx
# showed 1589 changed lines when the real change was 32.
#
# `text=auto` stores every file git detects as text with LF in the repository,
# while still checking it out with the platform's native endings.
* text=auto
# Executed or parsed on Linux: must stay LF whatever the checkout platform. A CRLF shell script fails
# with "$'\r': command not found"; a CRLF nginx include can fail to parse.
*.sh            text eol=lf
deploy/**       text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
